🎨 Program 17 -Real-Time Application : CAD Shape Drawing System

📌 Description

A Computer-Aided Design (CAD) application needs to handle different shapes such as circles, rectangles, and triangles.

Each shape has its own implementation of "draw()" and "area()". A common abstract base class called "Shape" provides the interface.

The program stores different shapes using base-class pointers and uses run-time polymorphism to call the appropriate functions.

🎯 OOP Concepts Used

- 🔹 Abstract class
- 🔹 Pure virtual functions
- 🔹 Inheritance
- 🔹 Run-time polymorphism
- 🔹 Function overriding
- 🔹 "std::unique_ptr"
- 🔹 Base-class pointers

💡 Key Point

Different shapes can be handled through the same "Shape" interface while each shape provides its own implementation of "draw()" and "area()".
